== 2. The fact the round rests on, in the code on main (Source) ==
handoff role rewrites the calling session's own binding whole (bind, cmd/handoff/session.go:
the final writeBinding has only the new role), so a session given reviewer-3 and then
reviewer-2 keeps no trace of having held reviewer-3. Round 8's "any binding that ever held
the seat at a later generation" could therefore miss it. Role moves are not entries in the
record, so the seat's last generation needs somewhere of its own to be kept.
